    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0790" n="504" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg504"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2704</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-07-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 7, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 3 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Danish Merchants’ Guild representative here has asked Guild not to submit further
                    applications for dried fruit import permits owing to excessive importations over
                    ration allotted by British Government; consequently not probable that further
                    dried fruit shipments will be allowed in Denmark until end this year.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
